NNAAMMEE
     nneexxttbboooott — specify an alternate kernel and boot flags for the next reboot

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     nneexxttbboooott [--aaff] [--ee _v_a_r_i_a_b_l_e_=_v_a_l_u_e] [--kk _k_e_r_n_e_l] [--oo _o_p_t_i_o_n_s]
     nneexxttbboooott --DD

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The nneexxttbboooott utility allows specifying some combination of an alternate
     kernel, boot flags, and kernel environment for the next time the machine
     is booted.  Once the loader(8) loads in the new kernel information from
     the _/_b_o_o_t_/_n_e_x_t_b_o_o_t_._c_o_n_f file, it is disabled so in case the new kernel
     hangs the machine, once it is rebooted, the machine will automatically
     revert to its previous configuration.

     The options are as follows:

     --aa          This option causes nneexxttbboooott to append to an existing configu‐
                 ration in _/_b_o_o_t_/_n_e_x_t_b_o_o_t_._c_o_n_f.  By default any existing con‐
                 figuration is overwritten.

     --DD          Invoking nneexxttbboooott with this option removes an existing
                 nneexxttbboooott configuration.

     --ee _v_a_r_i_a_b_l_e_=_v_a_l_u_e
                 This option adds the provided variable and value to the ker‐
                 nel environment.  The value is quoted when written to the
                 nneexxttbboooott configuration.

     --ff          This option disables the sanity checking which checks if the
                 kernel really exists before writing the nneexxttbboooott configura‐
                 tion.

     --kk _k_e_r_n_e_l   This option specifies a kernel directory relative to _/_b_o_o_t to
                 load the kernel and any modules from.

     --oo _o_p_t_i_o_n_s  This option allows the passing of kernel flags for the next
                 boot.

FFIILLEESS
     /boot/nextboot.conf  The configuration file that the nneexxttbboooott configura‐
                          tion is written into.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     To boot the _G_E_N_E_R_I_C kernel with the nneexxttbboooott command:

           nextboot -k GENERIC

     To enable into single user mode with the normal kernel:

           nextboot -o "-s" -k kernel

     To remove an existing nextboot configuration:

           nextboot -D

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     boot(8), freebsd-update(8), loader(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The original nneexxttbboooott manual page first appeared in FreeBSD 2.2.  It used
     a very different interface to achieve similar results.

     The current incarnation of nneexxttbboooott appeared in FreeBSD 5.0.

AAUUTTHHOORRSS
